'''''Sphenopus divaricatus''''' is a species of grass in the family [[Poaceae]] (true grasses).<ref>{{Cite web|title=Sphenopus divaricatus (Gouan) Rchb. - Encyclopedia of Life|url=https://eol.org/pages/5813768|access-date=2022-02-04|website=eol.org}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Mifsud |first=Stephen |date=2002-08-23 |title=Sphenopus divaricatus (Coastal Grass) : MaltaWildPlants.com - the online Flora of the Maltese Islands. |url=https://www.maltawildplants.com/POAC/Sphenopus_divaricatus.php |access-date=2022-03-07 |website=www.maltawildplants.com |language=en-us}}</ref> It is an [[annual plant|annual]] native to the [[Mediterranean Basin]] countries of North Africa, southern Europe, and western Asia and eastwards to Tajikistan, Kyrgyzstan, and Pakistan.<ref name = powo/>

